{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstring>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int K = 105, Mod = 1e9 + 7;\n\nstruct Mat {\n    int a[K][K];\n    Mat() { memset(a, 0, sizeof(a)); }\n    void unit(int len) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= len; ++i) a[i][i] = 1;\n    }\n};\n\nint k;\n\nint id(int x, int step) {\n    return x <= k ? ((x + step - 1) % k + 1) : x;\n}\n\nMat move_mat(const Mat &base, int step) {\n    step %= k;\n    Mat res;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k + 1; ++i)\n        for (int j = 1; j <= k + 1; ++j)\n            res.a[id(i, step)][id(j, step)] = base.a[i][j];\n    return res;\n}\n\nMat operator*(const Mat &lhs, const Mat &rhs) {\n    Mat res;\n    int cur = k + 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= cur; ++i)\n        for (int m = 1; m <= cur; ++m) if (lhs.a[i][m])\n            for (int j = 1; j <= cur; ++j)\n                res.a[i][j] = (res.a[i][j] + (ll)lhs.a[i][m] * rhs.a[m][j]) % Mod;\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ll n;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    Mat A[K];\n    A[0].unit(k + 1);\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k + 1; ++i) A[0].a[1][i] = 1;\n    vector<int> V;\n    int len = 0;\n    for (ll tmp = n; tmp; tmp /= k) {\n        V.push_back(tmp % k);\n        Mat x = A[len];\n        A[len + 1].unit(k + 1);\n        ll power = k;\n        int p = 0;\n        while (power) {\n            if (power & 1) A[len + 1] = A[len + 1] * move_mat(x, (power ^ 1) << p);\n            x = move_mat(x, 1 << p) * x;\n            power >>= 1;\n            ++p;\n        }\n        ++len;\n    }\n    int step = 0;\n    int ans[K] = {0};\n    ans[k + 1] = 1;\n    for (int T = (int)V.size() - 1; T >= 0; --T) {\n        int cur = V[T];\n        if (cur) {\n            int tmp[K];\n            for (int times = 0; times < cur; ++times) {\n                memcpy(tmp, ans, sizeof(tmp));\n                memset(ans, 0, sizeof(ans));\n                Mat B = move_mat(A[T], times + step);\n                for (int i = 1; i <= k + 1; ++i)\n                    for (int j = 1; j <= k + 1; ++j)\n                        ans[i] = (ans[i] + (ll)tmp[j] * B.a[i][j]) % Mod;\n            }\n        }\n        step += cur;\n    }\n    int res = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k + 1; ++i) res = (res + ans[i]) % Mod;\n    cout << res << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef id(x, step, k):\n    if x < k:\n        return (x + step) % k\n    else:\n        return k\n\nclass Mat:\n    def __init__(self, size):\n        self.size = size\n        self.a = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    def unit(self):\n        for i in range(self.size):\n            self.a[i][i] = 1\n    def __mul__(self, other):\n        n = self.size\n        res = Mat(n)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for m in range(n):\n                if self.a[i][m]:\n                    for j in range(n):\n                        res.a[i][j] = (res.a[i][j] + self.a[i][m] * other.a[m][j]) % MOD\n        return res\n\ndef move_mat(base, step, k):\n    step %= k\n    n = base.size\n    res = Mat(n)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            res.a[id(i, step, k)][id(j, step, k)] = base.a[i][j]\n    return res\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    size = k + 1\n\n    # Build base matrix A[0]\n    A = []\n    mat0 = Mat(size)\n    mat0.unit()\n    for i in range(size):\n        mat0.a[0][i] = 1\n    A.append(mat0)\n\n    # Digits in base k (least significant first)\n    V = []\n    tmp = n\n    while tmp:\n        V.append(tmp % k)\n        tmp //= k\n    # If n == 0, V is empty; handle later.\n\n    # Build A[1..len(V)]\n    for idx in range(len(V)):\n        x = A[idx]\n        next_mat = Mat(size)\n        next_mat.unit()\n        power = k\n        p = 0\n        while power:\n            if power & 1:\n                step = ((power ^ 1) << p) % k\n                next_mat = next_mat * move_mat(x, step, k)\n            step2 = (1 << p) % k\n            x = move_mat(x, step2, k) * x\n            power >>= 1\n            p += 1\n        A.append(next_mat)\n\n    # Process digits from most significant to least\n    step = 0\n    ans = [0] * size\n    ans[size - 1] = 1  # corresponds to index k+1 in 1-indexed\n    for T in range(len(V) - 1, -1, -1):\n        cur = V[T]\n        if cur:\n            for times in range(cur):\n                tmp = ans[:]\n                ans = [0] * size\n                B = move_mat(A[T], (times + step) % k, k)\n                for i in range(size):\n                    s = 0\n                    for j in range(size):\n                        s = (s + tmp[j] * B.a[i][j]) % MOD\n                    ans[i] = s\n        step += cur\n\n    res = sum(ans) % MOD\n    print(res)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.649054244509898e-